Weight heterogeneity at fixed raw support
n = 6000, target median raw support = 60, permutations per profile = 200, seed = 20261109

profile       b    n_B    S_B    e_B  e_row  sd(CEQ) sd(CEQ2) sd*sqrt(e_B)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
binary   0.0269   60.0  60.00   60.0  121.0   0.0029   0.0027    0.0227
gauss    0.0269   60.0  13.11   26.4   52.9   0.0035   0.0014    0.0182
sharp    0.0269   60.0   3.24    7.1   13.9   0.0060   0.0048    0.0160
jitter   0.0269   60.0  34.44    8.6   13.9   0.0088   0.0087    0.0258

sd(CEQ) varies by a factor of about 3.0 across profiles while the raw
support is identical (60 in all four) and the effective size varies from
7.1 to 60.0. sd*sqrt(e_B) stays within 0.0160 to 0.0258, so the scale of the
variance is the effective size and not the number of non-zero weights.

